        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_987197435.1",
        "comments": "The assembly ddLepDrab1.hap4.1 is based on 135x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Hi-C analysis indicates an octaploid genome comprising two distinguishable sets of four broadly similar haplotypes, consistent with an allooctaploidy. The assembly was partitioned into four primary assemblies (hap1?hap4), each containing one haplotype from each identified set. Further genetic analysis would be required to resolve the relationships among the chromosome copies. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 8 (9,950 - 10,949 Kbp) are uncertain. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 9 (10,581 ? 11,429 Kbp) are uncertain. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 10 (10,173 ? 12,219 Kbp) are uncertain. The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on chromosome 16 (7,122? 9,610 Kbp) are uncertain.",
